concall","as_of":"H1FY26"},"guidance":{"title":"Guidance","body":"Revenue growth: 7-8% YoY; EBITDA margin: Targeting 7-8% by FY28; Order inflow: No explicit guidance; Capex/Commissioning: ₹55cr for backward dyeing unit (Dec’26/Jan’27); ₹8-9cr for renewable energy (Q1FY27)","src":"concall","as_of":"H1FY26"},"growth_optionality":{"title":"Growth verticals / optionality","body":"Potential diversification into non-denim technical fabrics if denim demand softens; no B2C or brand launch planned; capacity expansion contingent on integration ROI","src":"concall","as_of":"H1FY26"},"margins":{"title":"Margins & cost dynamics","body":"Current EBITDA margin 2.6% due to pricing compromise to maintain working capital; dyeing integration expected to add ₹12cr PAT; renewable energy to save ₹4.5-4.65cr annually (from ₹2.65cr today); cost advantage from 65% renewable power, zero debt, and wider looms (82-inch) lowers unit cost vs peers","src":"concall","as_of":"H1FY26"},"capital_allocation":{"title":"Capital allocation","body":"Prioritizing capex for vertical integration and renewable energy; no dividends or buybacks mentioned; net debt equity at 0.11x provides flexibility; excess cash deployed in bonds and AIF for other income","src":"concall","as_of":"H1FY26"},"management_tone":{"title":"Management quality / tone","body":"Confident and structured; focused on execution of integration roadmap; transparent on margin compression being temporary; emphasizes working capital discipline and zero debt as competitive advantages; avoids overpromising on volume growth","src":"concall","as_of":"H1FY26"},"risks":{"title":"Risks & watch-items","body":"Pricing pressure from global tariffs and domestic competition; execution delay in dyeing unit commissioning; skill shortages during festive seasons; reliance on top 10 dealers for 99% revenue; no PLI benefits; margin expansion dependent on successful integration","src":"concall","as_of":"H1FY26"},"non_obvious":{"title":"Non-obvious takeaways","body":"Teesta Spintex’s ₹3.37cr profit in H1 is largely from job work (30% of sales), not internal fabric conversion — meaning integration benefits are not yet fully captured in consolidated margins; the 82-inch loom advantage is a hidden differentiator in a market dominated by 210cm looms; AIF investment in equity markets adds non-operational income volatility","src":"concall","as_of":"H1FY26"},"challenges":{"title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers","body":"| Challenge | Beneficiary/Loser | Dir | Conviction | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Shanti Spintex’s margin compression due to pricing compromise | Shanti Spintex Limited | beneficiary | High | Backward integration will eliminate ₹8-10/meter external dyeing costs, directly boosting PAT by ₹12cr |\n| Competitors with higher debt and fossil-fuel power costs | Arvind Mills; Nandan Denim | loser | Medium | Shanti’s zero-debt and 65% renewable power create 15-20% cost advantage; peers lack similar vertical integration |","src":"concall","as_of":"H1FY26"}}}